The Seto Congress has sent an appeal to the PM, urging the government to introduce compensation measures to support Setomaa, which would be adversely affected by Estonia closing its land border with Russia.
"The closure of border crossing points will have a direct economic impact on businesses operating in Setomaa Municipality as it will reduce economic activity throughout the region, people's purchasing power and the municipality's ability to provide essential services to residents," the Council of Elders of the Seto Congress (SKVK) said in its appeal. "This, in turn, will lead to a deterioration in living conditions for Setomaa residents and could cause people to leave the area, further increasing security risks for Estonia," Seto leaders said in the appeal sent Tuesday.
